::GEO_U04_L04_Q16::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U04_L04_Q16<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.SIM.1<br><br>Question:<br>Which proportion correctly solves for x when corresponding sides are 4 to 10 and 6 to x? {
~A. <sup>4</sup>&frasl;<sub>6</sub> = <sup>10</sup>&frasl;<sub>x</sub>#This compares sides from different figures in the first ratio and can mismatch correspondence.
~B. 4 + 10 = 6 + x#Similar figures require multiplicative ratios, not additive equations.
~C. 4x = 6#This omits the corresponding side length 10 and does not represent the proportion.
=D. <sup>4</sup>&frasl;<sub>10</sub> = <sup>6</sup>&frasl;<sub>x</sub>#Corresponding sides must be matched in the same order in both ratios.
}

